{
  "_comment": "Where the holders of the non-ICB agreements that permit sublicensing record what happens to the data next. One entry per holder, naming its agreements by base reference. `kind` is `sub-licensees` for a list of organisations the data was passed on to, `approved uses` for a register of projects approved to use it, usually inside the holder's own trusted research environment, and `publications` for the holder's own list of papers. `nhs_england_only: true` marks a list of NHS England data only; every other list covers all of the holder's data, and the page says so. `source` is the holder's page that links a register kept elsewhere. `opened: false` marks a page found by search that refuses requests from the build environment, so it was not opened. Notes are shown to readers. Collected by hand; check with `python -m pipeline.onward`.",
  "checked": "2026-11-07",
